From fc76629874300b4454b093c3aea96a1898dc8f80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: assistant <a@a.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0135: Melee/Ranged/Caster Hero Roles

- Role type (melee/ranged/caster), Hero.role/unlockedRoles (optional,
  no migration needed), RaidDef.requiredRoles, RoleDef.
- All 9 hero classes get native role + roleFlavors naming table;
  Gladiator reassigned to Ranged (confirmed via sprite art).
- Training system: HeroManager.roleCost/trainRole, two-tier cost
  (higher one-time unlock per role, small repeatable swap cost between
  already-unlocked roles). HeroesPanel gets a role chip row; hero card
  summary line now shows the trained role's flavour name.
- Raid party composition only, not board/chain quest math (deliberate
  scope decision from the backlog discussion). RaidManager.
  partyRoleCounts/roleMismatchPenalty fold a flat per-unmet-slot
  penalty into the existing partySuccessBonus formula. RaidsPanel gets
  RoleRequirementCircle (mirrors DifficultyCircle, green check overlay
  on met slots), live off the current party selection.
- DevTool: new 'roles' content type (icon field reuses the existing
  picker, zero new backend code for icons themselves), hero-classes
  gains role/roleFlavors fields, raids gains requiredRoles -- two new
  field types (roleFlavors, roleRequirements), all three verified with
  real POST round-trips plus three deliberate negative-validation
  tests.
- Also fixed: devtool's MOD_KEYS (server.mjs + app.js) was never
  updated for the 5 Modifiers keys added in patch 0133 (Vendor
  Upgrades Consolidation) -- fixed alongside this patch.
- Rebased twice mid-build as main moved (0133's status.md append point,
  then again after a Tutorial Quest/buyback patch landed); final
  version applied cleanly and compiles clean against current main.
- guild-idler-status.md updated.
